# magic_isomorphic_keyboard, checked headless (`zig build magic-isomorphic-keyboard-check`), in C major with the tonic C
# on the F key and fifths along the rows: for each window of the run, in seconds, the pitch classes that must sound -
# every other must be silent - and the loudness, as RMS, the left channel. A Shepard note at velocity 0.5, centred, is
# 0.3755 x 0.5 x 0.7071 = 0.1328; three of them, whose partials all differ, 0.1328 x sqrt 3 = 0.2300. Each window
# starts 0.1 s into a hold and ends 0.05 s before its release. The keys: F, G, V, H, D alone, then the triangles
# F G V (C major), F T G (C minor), J I K (A minor), G H B (G major).
#
# start  end    notes      rms
0.20   0.45   C          0.1328
1.20   1.45   G          0.1328
2.20   2.45   E          0.1328
3.20   3.45   D          0.1328
4.20   4.45   F          0.1328
5.20   5.45   C E G      0.2300
6.20   6.45   C D# G     0.2300
7.20   7.45   A C E      0.2300
8.20   8.45   G B D      0.2300
